{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_ae44e878a6d3",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 203,
      "mechanism": "In the EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE (line ~5995-6020), the code asserts input_axis_tready_next = 1 and loads the first word into temp registers when input_axis_tvalid is asserted. If input_axis_tlast accompanies that word, the adapter should not immediately offer another ready to the source because the output side may not yet be ready to accept the corresponding byte. The patch adds (input_axis_tlast) to the gate so that ready is only asserted when the incoming frame is not terminating, preventing premature acceptance that causes input_axis_tready to stay low (actual 0) at cycle 8 and output_axis_tvalid to leak high (actual 1) at cycle 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4da73638e1ac",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 250,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_TRANSFER_IN (line ~9435-9450) the transition to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT fires when the cycle counter hits CYCLE_COUNT-1 or input_axis_tlast. The patch additionally requires output_axis_tready_int, ensuring the output pipeline can accept the first output word before the state machine commits to emitting it. Without this guard the adapter transitions to output while the output register file is still full, so input_axis_tready remains de-asserted (cycle 8 actual 0) and output_axis_tlast is not driven correctly."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_3cb99864f502",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 185,
      "mechanism": "In the same EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE, after capturing a word with tlast the code immediately sets state_next = STATE_TRANSFER_OUT and input_axis_tready_next = output_axis_tready_int_early. The patch qualifies the tlast check with output_axis_tready_int so the adapter only commits to the output phase when the output side is ready. This directly addresses the cycle-8 input_axis_tready mismatch and the cycle-9 output_axis_tvalid spur."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_0517c5c2c927",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 148,
      "mechanism": "The combinational block unconditionally defaults input_axis_tready_next = 0 at line ~5049. When none of the explicit assignments in a state branch are taken (e.g., output not ready in STATE_TRANSFER_OUT), ready falls to 0 instead of holding its previous value. Retaining input_axis_tready_reg preserves back-pressure semantics and keeps input_axis_tready high at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2809cde8141f",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 173,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_IDLE CYCLE_COUNT==1 path (line ~5967-5985) the adapter passes input_axis_tvalid straight to output_axis_tvalid_int without checking input_axis_tlast. If the incoming word is an end-of-frame, the output register file may not be ready, yet the state machine assumes it can accept another word next cycle. Qualifying with input_axis_tlast prevents this optimistic ready assertion."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e1b071d54052",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 153,
      "mechanism": "The CYCLE_COUNT==1 entry condition (line ~5165) is gated only by the static parameter. The patch adds a dynamic input_axis_tvalid requirement so the adapter does not enter the passthrough path when the source is not actually valid, avoiding a spurious ready pulse that desynchronizes the pipeline."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_7d6c69bf2e61",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 220,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_TRANSFER_OUT EXPAND_BUS branch (line ~8232-8254) the transition back to STATE_TRANSFER_IN or STATE_IDLE after output_axis_tready_int fires checks input_axis_tready & input_axis_tvalid. The patch adds input_axis_tvalid to the gate, ensuring the adapter only tries to fetch the next input word when the source is actually presenting one, which stabilizes the ready handshake at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_585622aac098",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 173,
      "mechanism": "In the EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE (line ~5967-6020) the first-word capture is gated by input_axis_tvalid alone. The patch adds !input_axis_tlast so that a terminating frame does not immediately trigger the fill-and-forward sequence; instead the adapter waits for output_axis_tready_int, preventing the cycle-8 ready dropout and cycle-9 valid leak."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "All eight candidates target the handshake logic around the EXPAND_BUS path (64-bit to 8-bit) where the public failure manifests: input_axis_tready de-asserts at cycle 8 (actual 0, expected 1), output_axis_tlast stays low at cycle 8, and output_axis_tvalid spuriously asserts at cycle 9. The patches qualify combinational conditions with nearby scalar signals (input_axis_tlast, output_axis_tready_int, input_axis_tvalid) or retain prior ready state, directly addressing the premature state transitions and ready defaults that the trace shows. Static dependency analysis confirms each edit touches the failing signals’ transitive fan-in within the 150-343 line window."
}
